      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do you put the socket under a specific out directory? My understanding is that it\u0027s going to be shared with other build directories/other projects.\n\ne.g. \n```\nautoninja -C out/foo # start a collector with out/foo/otel_collector.sock\nautoninja -C out/bar # try to start a collector with out/bar/otel_collector.sock\n```\n\nSo, I think the socket file needs to be a globally unique path.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 328,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 329,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "51511279932def07d0790be5880d1ea5b080cd08",
