      "writtenOn": "2025-12-07T23:31:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually no, the whole reason we went for sockets is for users not to step on each other toes when they are on a same machine. So each user, or each build rather, will have their own sockets file. The previous design was to have one port, which would have this problem of connections congestion.\n\nOne thing I realize is that it generally should be impossible to run multiple collector instances though because we are expecting the same health port. So we kind of still congesting on the same socket file. We can discuss this later as well, we can remove the sockets code without much issues later.",
      "parentUuid": "65cbb753_73e137fd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 328,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 329,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "51511279932def07d0790be5880d1ea5b080cd08",
